==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{confix|anthropo|sophy}}, from a Renaissance Latin ''anthroposophia'' (attested in Heinrich Cornelius Agrippa, d. 1535 and Thomas Vaughan, d. 1666), popularized from the 1910s via German  ''Anthroposophie'' ([[:w:Rudolf Steiner|Rudolf Steiner]], 1861–1925).

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}
# Human wisdom; knowledge or understanding of human nature. 
# A spiritual movement inaugurated by Rudolf Steiner (also capitalized as [[Anthroposophy]]).

